# OneWoW QoL External Modules

A QoL module is a self-contained folder under `OneWoW_QoL/Modules/external/<id>/`.
The hub handles registration, the Features UI, toggles, saved state, and language
switching — your folder just declares metadata and logic.

**Full guide: `OneWoW_QoL/DEVELOPERS.md`** (folder layout, every module/toggle
field, lifecycle callbacks, categories, SavedVariables). This rule is the
load-bearing subset — the handful of conventions that cause bugs when missed.

## The five rules that bite

1. **`module.lua` loads FIRST and is the only home of the module `id`.** It calls
   `ns.ModuleRegistry:Define(ADDON_NAME, { id = "yourmodule", ... })` — metadata
   only, no logic, no frames. `Define` registers the module, derives its locale
   scope, and caches the view. List `module.lua` at the top of your TOC block,
   before locale and code files. There is no `data.lua`.

2. **`Current()` is load-time only.** Every other file opens with
   `local M, L = ns.ModuleRegistry:Current()` captured into a file-local at the top.
   It returns "the module currently loading" — call it once per file, never at
   runtime (by then a different module may be loading). Variants:
   `local _, L = ...:Current()` (strings only), `local M = ...:Current()` (no
   strings), or skip the call entirely if a file needs neither.

3. **Cross-module access goes through the registry, never a global.** Use
   `ns.ModuleRegistry:GetById("minimapbuttons")`. There is no `ns.YourModule`
   global — it was removed. Within your own files, use the local from `Current()`.

4. **Locale scope is `M._scope` (`ADDON_NAME .. "." .. id`).** Locale files register
   into it: `OneWoW.Locale:Register(M._scope, "enUS", { KEY = "text" })`. Store key
   names in `title`/`description`/toggle `label` — the Features UI resolves them
   from your scope. enUS folds first, active language on top (omitted koKR keys
   fall back to English).

5. **No `L[key] or "fallback"` literals.** A missing key already resolves to its own
   name, so the miss is visible. For genuinely optional text use
   `OneWoW.Locale:GetOptional(scope, key)`. (Suite-wide Locale contract:
   `OneWoW/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §6.)

## Reference module

`Modules/external/autodelete/` is a complete, multi-file module — copy its shape.
